{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-qccp-gfcp-xxvc","cve_id":"CVE-2026-44431","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-qccp-gfcp-xxvc","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qccp-gfcp-xxvc","summary":"urllib3: Sensitive headers forwarded across origins in proxied low-level redirects","description":"### Impact\n\nWhen following cross-origin redirects for requests made using urllib3’s high-level APIs, such as `urllib3.request()`, `PoolManager.request()`, and `ProxyManager.request()`, sensitive headers — `Authorization`, `Cookie`, and `Proxy-Authorization` (defined in `Retry.DEFAULT_REMOVE_HEADERS_ON_REDIRECT`) — are stripped by default, as expected.\n\nHowever, cross-origin redirects followed from the low-level API via `ProxyManager.connection_from_url().urlopen(..., assert_same_host=False)` still forward these sensitive headers.\n\n### Affected usage\n\nApplications and libraries using urllib3 versions earlier than 2.7.0 may be affected if they allow cross-origin redirects while making requests through `HTTPConnection.urlopen()` instances created via `ProxyManager.connection_from_url()`.\n\n### Remediation\n\nUpgrade to urllib3 version 2.7.0 or later, in which sensitive headers are stripped from redirects followed by `HTTPConnection`.\n\nIf upgrading is not immediately possible, avoid using this low-level redirect flow for cross-origin redirects. If appropriate for your use case, switch to `ProxyManager.request()`.","type":"reviewed","severity":"high","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urllib3/urllib3/security-advisories/GHSA-qccp-gfcp-xxvc","source_code_location":"https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-qccp-gfcp-xxvc","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-44431","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/security/advisories/GHSA-qccp-gfcp-xxvc","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-44431","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qccp-gfcp-xxvc"],"published_at":"2026-05-11T14:51:20Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T20:35:54Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-05-11T14:51:20Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-05-13T16:16:57Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"urllib3"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 1.23, < 2.7.0","first_patched_version":"2.7.0","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N","score":5.3},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","score":8.2}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-200","name":"Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login":"christos-cantina-security","id":265288016,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8_5UA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265288016?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/christos-cantina-security","html_url":"https://github.com/christos-cantina-security","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christos-cantina-security/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christos-cantina-security/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christos-cantina-security/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christos-cantina-security/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christos-cantina-security/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christos-cantina-security/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christos-cantina-security/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christos-cantina-security/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christos-cantina-security/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"reporter"},{"user":{"login":"illia-v","id":17710133,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzEwMTMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17710133?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/illia-v","html_url":"https://gith